course: dictionary
lesson: 14713
title: A formal word: procurable
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Procurable is a formal word. It means able to be got, bought or obtained. «Spare parts for the old bike are procurable at the shop on the corner.» The clues are the shop and the parts: they can be bought there, so procurable means can be got.
explain: Formal words often appear in letters, reports, adverts and stories about shortages or adventures. «Clean water was hardly procurable after the flood.» The words hardly and flood tell you that getting clean water was difficult, so procurable can mean available, often with some effort.
explain: Test your meaning in the sentence. Put in "able to be got" and check: «Clean water was hardly able to be got» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. When a word sounds grand, look for a simpler word it is close to, such as available or get.
fact: Procurable is an adjective, a word that describes a thing.
fact: Procurable means able to be got, bought or obtained.
fact: Procure means to get, and -able means can be, so procurable means can be got.
fact: «Available» and «obtainable» are close in meaning, but procurable is more formal.
fact: «Readily procurable» and «easily procurable» mean very easy to get; «not procurable» means you cannot get it at all.
exercise: «The rare stamp is no longer procurable in any shop.» What does procurable mean here? | Wrapped up tight | Very large and heavy | Shiny and new | *Able to be got or bought
exercise: «Fresh fish is easily procurable by the harbour.» Which word is closest in meaning to procurable? | Empty | Hidden | Broken | *Available
exercise: «Ice cream was not procurable at the fair.» What does this tell you? | There was far too much to choose from | *Nobody could get any to buy | It was free for everyone
test: «Spare parts were not procurable in the small village.» What does procurable mean? | Old and worn | Full of people | *Able to be got, bought or obtained | Very loud
test: Which phrase means very easy to get? | not procurable | barely a whisper | *readily procurable | ancient and grey
exam: «Tickets were procurable at the gate.» Which word means the same as procurable? | *Available | Free | Hidden | Heavy
